Cover at minimum 10 risks across these categories:
- **Technical**: Architecture doesn't scale, integration failures, data migration issues, security vulnerabilities
- **Team**: Key person leaves, hiring delays, skill gaps, burnout
- **Timeline**: Scope creep, dependency delays, underestimation, external blockers
- **Market**: Competitor launches first, market shifts, regulatory changes
- **Financial**: Budget overrun, funding delay, unit economics don't work
- **Operational**: Infrastructure outage, data loss, compliance failure

For the top 3 risks: detailed mitigation plan with specific actions, owners, and timelines.

# 6. Launch Plan & Go-To-Market Alignment

### Pre-Launch Checklist
- [ ] All P0 features complete and tested
- [ ] Performance benchmarks met (specify: p95 < Xms, throughput > X rps)
- [ ] Security audit passed (penetration test, dependency scan)
- [ ] Monitoring and alerting configured with runbooks
- [ ] Support documentation and FAQs ready
- [ ] Legal review complete (ToS, privacy policy, cookie policy)
- [ ] Analytics and tracking implemented
- [ ] Backup and disaster recovery tested
- [ ] On-call rotation established with escalation paths
- [ ] Marketing assets ready (landing page, launch email, social)

### Beta Testing Strategy
- Beta cohort size and selection criteria
- Feedback collection tools and process
- Bug triage and response SLA during beta
- Go/no-go criteria for GA based on beta results

### Launch Day Plan
- Hour-by-hour timeline for launch day
- War room setup and communication channels
- Rollback criteria and procedure
- Post-launch monitoring dashboard

### Post-Launch (First 30 Days)
- Daily standups → weekly as stability improves
- User feedback triage and response process
- Hot-fix deployment process
- Success criteria for "launch was successful"

# 7. Communication & Governance

- **Stakeholder updates**: Weekly status report template, monthly steering committee
- **Team ceremonies**: Daily standup, sprint planning, retro, backlog grooming — cadence and duration
- **Decision framework**: RACI for key decisions (architecture, hiring, scope changes, budget)
- **Scope change process**: How to evaluate and approve scope changes without derailing timeline
- **Escalation path**: When and how to escalate blockers

# 8. Success Metrics & Review Cadence

| Phase | KPI | Target | Review Frequency | Owner |
|-------|-----|--------|-----------------|-------|

- **Weekly**: Sprint velocity, bug count, deployment frequency
- **Monthly**: Feature completion vs plan, budget burn rate, team health
- **Quarterly**: Product metrics (users, retention, revenue), roadmap review, team retro
- **Pivot criteria**: What numbers at what point trigger a strategy review?

